{"availability":"available","full":"mFurkanHiz/opscommerce-showcase","name":"opscommerce-showcase","description":"Operations-first commerce platform — order lifecycle, ATP inventory, courier fulfillment, RMA and production. Curated showcase: domain core (tested in CI), architecture docs and live demo.","category":"Design","language":"C#","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-27T16:04:23Z","updated":"2026-07-27T17:43:02Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://opscommerce-demo.rapidconfigs.com","topics":["aspnetcore","clean-architecture","csharp","ddd","dotnet","ecommerce","inventory-management","multi-tenant","nextjs","order-management","portfolio","state-machine","warehouse-management","xunit"],"demo":"https://opscommerce-demo.rapidconfigs.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.068Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.068Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.068Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.068Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An operations-first commerce platform — not just a storefront, but the full engine behind it: order lifecycle, deposit-based payments, warehouse inventory with overselling protection, courier delivery, returns (RMA), production orders and a complete operational audit trail.","About this repository. OpsCommerce is a private, full-stack project. This public repository is a curated showcase: it contains the complete domain core — it compiles, and its tests run in CI on every push (see the badge) — plus the architecture and data-model documentation and commented highlights from the service layer. The full application (API, frontend, infrastructure) is private. See LICENSE.","Most demo shops stop at \"add to cart, pay, done\". Real commerce is won or lost after the payment: who reserves the stock, which warehouse ships it, which courier carries it, what happens when the customer returns it. OpsCommerce is built around that operational side:"],"features":["A seller can allow deposit-based selling per product (pay 30% now, the balance later).","A warehouse worker sees stock with Available-To-Promise numbers and moves goods between warehouses.","A courier gets assigned deliveries and advances them step by step on their own screen.","A customer manages addresses, tracks orders and opens return/exchange/repair requests.","Every action lands in an audit trail, so any order can be replayed as a step-by-step story:"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mFurkanHiz/opscommerce-showcase/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f2635353048621fdfd2b0e359709ef4e22c5d3b819fb4e02d4f38a51c69558c9","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.221Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.221Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An operations-first commerce platform — not just a storefront, but the full engine behind it: order lifecycle, deposit-based payments, warehouse inventory with overselling protection, courier delivery, returns (RMA), production orders and a complete operational audit trail.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mFurkanHiz/opscommerce-showcase/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"More: storefront · login with demo roles · management dashboard · RMA management","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mFurkanHiz/opscommerce-showcase/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"No credentials to copy: the sign-in page has a \"Sign in with a demo role\" panel — pick a role and it logs you in.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mFurkanHiz/opscommerce-showcase/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f2635353048621fdfd2b0e359709ef4e22c5d3b819fb4e02d4f38a51c69558c9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mFurkanHiz/opscommerce-showcase/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.221Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-27T17:43:02Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github